# Build-context exclusions for docker build (deploy/docker/*.Dockerfile).
# Context is the monorepo root; no need to drag in .git/local artifacts.
.git
.gitignore
.pm
.claude
*/bin/
bin/
dev
docs
examples
*.md
.dockerignore
deploy

# ...except the two cross-compiled artifacts the L3c images are made of.
# deploy/docker/keeper.Dockerfile compiles inside the builder stage and needs
# nothing from bin/; tests/e2e-k8s/dockerfiles/*.Dockerfile COPY the output of
# `make build-linux` directly, and share this file because they share the root
# build context. Without these two lines `make docker-build-keeper` fails on
# "keeper/bin/keeper-linux-amd64: not found" and L3c cannot be built at all -
# which is where it has been since the beta (NIM-490 found it while wiring the
# image provenance check; the tier is loudly broken rather than falsely green,
# but a pre-flight for an image nobody can build guards nothing).
!keeper/bin/keeper-linux-amd64
!soul/bin/soul-linux-amd64
